WEBVTT

00:00:10.219 --> 00:00:13.889
What happens if I die here?

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:32.199
I bet no one would notice I was gone.
It's not like I have any friends.

00:00:32.199 --> 00:00:36.370
Only the school administrators would care

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:39.623
and only after they notice
my tuition hasn't been paid,

00:00:39.623 --> 00:00:44.461
and then maybe student services

00:00:44.461 --> 00:00:48.465
once they realize I haven't
paid back my student loan.

00:00:48.465 --> 00:00:55.264
But soon, it will...

00:00:56.932 --> 00:01:01.895
It will all... be over.

00:01:05.774 --> 00:01:08.527
Is somebody there?

00:01:08.527 --> 00:01:08.861
--A human?

00:01:08.861 --> 00:01:10.028
--Is that you, Satsuki?
--A human?

00:01:10.028 --> 00:01:11.864
--Is that you, Satsuki?

00:01:14.324 --> 00:01:17.536
No? Then who's there? Are you human?

00:01:17.536 --> 00:01:19.621
Do you need help? Or are you--

00:01:19.621 --> 00:01:23.542
I-I'm human! Help--

00:01:23.542 --> 00:01:26.712
Careful! That thing's dangerous!

00:01:26.712 --> 00:01:28.005
What's dangerous?

00:01:28.005 --> 00:01:33.886
I-It's all white and wiggly.
Whatever you do, don't look at it!

00:01:47.566 --> 00:01:50.444
It's so beautiful.

00:01:50.444 --> 00:01:56.617
It's all golden... It's as if... as if...

00:02:12.216 --> 00:02:14.009
I thought you were Ophelia.

00:02:14.009 --> 00:02:16.261
Huh?

00:02:16.261 --> 00:02:18.639
What?

00:02:18.639 --> 00:02:22.893
Um, hey, wait!

00:02:30.317 --> 00:02:31.735
I-I feel sick.

00:02:31.735 --> 00:02:35.864
I told you. Just looking
at that thing is bad news.

00:02:35.864 --> 00:02:37.032
When did you say that?

00:02:37.032 --> 00:02:40.077
You should try listening.

00:02:40.077 --> 00:02:43.413
What if you keep looking at it?

00:02:43.413 --> 00:02:45.832
I have no idea.

00:03:00.305 --> 00:03:01.348
Huh?

00:03:01.348 --> 00:03:02.558
It's gone.

00:03:02.558 --> 00:03:04.935
Did I do that? It hit, didn't it?

00:03:04.935 --> 00:03:07.229
Yeah. What did you throw at it?

00:03:07.229 --> 00:03:08.939
A chunk of rock salt!

00:03:08.939 --> 00:03:11.650
I heard it works on those things,
so I always wanted to try it.

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:13.652
Guess it's true!

00:03:17.948 --> 00:03:19.700
Thanks.

00:03:23.996 --> 00:03:27.165
Wow, that was creepy, huh?

00:03:27.165 --> 00:03:29.960
Um, thanks for saving me.

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:32.629
I'm Toriko Nishina. What's your name?

00:03:32.629 --> 00:03:35.299
Oh, um, I'm Sorawo Kamikoshi--

00:03:35.299 --> 00:03:38.468
Sorawo, did you enter this side near here?

00:03:38.468 --> 00:03:40.053
Yeah, really close by.

00:03:40.053 --> 00:03:44.141
That's a relief! Actually, I'm lost.

00:03:44.141 --> 00:03:47.561
One second. I'm gonna go get that salt I threw.

00:03:48.604 --> 00:03:51.106
Hmm?

00:04:50.541 --> 00:04:51.708
"Kisaragi"
"Katasu - Yami"

00:05:40.883 --> 00:05:43.135
"No. 1 Shopping Mall"

00:05:43.135 --> 00:05:44.761
"Famous Kushikatsu Naka"

00:05:44.761 --> 00:05:46.847
"No bicycling"

00:05:48.015 --> 00:05:51.852
How many times have you been to that world?

00:05:51.852 --> 00:05:53.478
Maybe, like, ten times.

00:05:53.478 --> 00:05:55.314
That many?

00:05:55.314 --> 00:05:59.568
Oh, that explains why you're an expert.
And you fought off that wiggle-waggle.

00:05:59.568 --> 00:06:03.947
Wiggle-waggle? You mean that
white thing? That's what it's called?

00:06:03.947 --> 00:06:07.743
That's just what I heard.

00:06:07.743 --> 00:06:11.413
Interesting. Who's the expert now?

00:06:11.413 --> 00:06:15.334
It's just, I've read about it before.

00:06:15.334 --> 00:06:20.839
But I never thought it was real.

00:06:20.839 --> 00:06:26.220
The wiggle-waggle urban legend
dates back to around 2003,

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:28.388
mostly on the net.

00:06:28.388 --> 00:06:33.018
It looks like a white shadow
that wiggles and dances about.

00:06:33.018 --> 00:06:37.439
Those who see it go mad. That about sums it up.

00:06:37.439 --> 00:06:44.530
Hmm, I see. And what about this thing
I picked up. You know what it is?

00:06:51.995 --> 00:06:58.210
What <i>is </i>this? It reflects everything but us.
It's creeping me out.

00:06:58.210 --> 00:07:01.296
Interesting.

00:07:01.296 --> 00:07:03.298
How much could we get for it?

00:07:03.298 --> 00:07:05.968
Are you crazy? We don't even know what it is.

00:07:05.968 --> 00:07:08.136
And was it a good idea
to bring it from that side?

00:07:08.136 --> 00:07:11.139
That side? You mean the world on the other side?

00:07:11.139 --> 00:07:13.475
That's what you call it?

00:07:13.475 --> 00:07:16.812
That's just what I call it.

00:07:16.812 --> 00:07:22.359
Our world is this side,
so the other world is that side.

00:07:22.359 --> 00:07:28.365
I call it the Otherside.
Did you see anyone over there?

00:07:28.365 --> 00:07:33.078
No. You're the first person
I ever met on that side.

00:07:34.246 --> 00:07:36.248
I see.

00:07:37.875 --> 00:07:39.877
Are you looking for somebody?

00:07:39.877 --> 00:07:43.130
Come to think of it, you mentioned someone.

00:07:43.130 --> 00:07:45.799
Satsuki or something.

00:07:56.059 --> 00:07:58.187
What should we do?

00:08:13.202 --> 00:08:15.370
What is that?

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:17.539
What's happening, Sorawo?

00:08:17.539 --> 00:08:23.837
Nothing. It's just all blue.

00:08:23.837 --> 00:08:25.631
Get back!

00:08:25.631 --> 00:08:26.965
I-Is that a gun?

00:08:26.965 --> 00:08:30.135
Relax. It's just a Makarov.

00:08:31.637 --> 00:08:35.516
So it was all blue out there?

00:08:35.516 --> 00:08:37.476
Y-Yeah.

00:08:37.476 --> 00:08:39.686
Okay.

00:08:44.316 --> 00:08:46.693
Huh?

00:08:51.823 --> 00:08:55.702
Whew, that really had me worried!

00:08:55.702 --> 00:09:00.666
I guess that entrance
can't be used anymore. Huh?

00:09:00.666 --> 00:09:05.337
Hey, Sorawo. What's wrong?

00:09:06.421 --> 00:09:13.178
Don't look so disappointed! Next time,
I'll take you to where I went, okay?

00:09:13.178 --> 00:09:15.973
No, I'm good.

00:09:15.973 --> 00:09:21.562
What was that blue thing?
It made you draw your gun.

00:09:21.562 --> 00:09:26.859
I've heard of it. That world is full of dangers,

00:09:26.859 --> 00:09:29.736
but the most dangerous is
when everything turns blue.

00:09:29.736 --> 00:09:32.948
Something even scarier is gonna attack us?

00:09:32.948 --> 00:09:36.910
I don't know. I'm new to all this, too.

00:09:38.537 --> 00:09:42.541
Enough of this! Let's call it a day
and get a fresh start tomorrow.

00:09:42.541 --> 00:09:44.376
Hey, what's your number?

00:09:44.376 --> 00:09:45.544
What?

00:09:45.544 --> 00:09:49.464
I never memorized my number,
and I didn't bring my phone today.

00:09:49.464 --> 00:09:55.846
Oh, my phone! What a relief. It's not broken.

00:09:57.306 --> 00:10:00.893
Wh-What is this?

00:10:02.561 --> 00:10:03.187
"Saitama University"

00:10:03.187 --> 00:10:06.481
"Saitama University"
The next time I ran into
Toriko was a week later.

00:10:07.191 --> 00:10:10.903
Sorawo! Hey there!

00:10:18.035 --> 00:10:20.454
Sorawo, don't you eat lunch with someone?

00:10:20.454 --> 00:10:23.624
It's none of your business!

00:10:23.624 --> 00:10:26.043
Why'd I do that?

00:10:26.043 --> 00:10:29.630
I didn't tell you my number or email address.

00:10:29.630 --> 00:10:32.799
Right. But you did tell me where
you went to school, remember?

00:10:32.799 --> 00:10:35.344
I found it in no time.

00:10:35.344 --> 00:10:40.098
I can't believe she found me
and actually showed up here.

00:10:40.098 --> 00:10:42.726
Hey, wanna go again?

00:10:42.726 --> 00:10:43.769
To that side?

00:10:43.769 --> 00:10:46.021
Mm-hmm.

00:10:46.021 --> 00:10:47.940
Go by yourself.

00:10:47.940 --> 00:10:51.068
Let's go together!

00:10:54.404 --> 00:10:55.405
"Investigating Japanese Ruins"

00:10:55.405 --> 00:10:56.114
"Investigating Japanese Ruins"
Is that a no?

00:10:56.657 --> 00:11:00.035
It's not a matter of yes or no.

00:11:00.035 --> 00:11:04.665
Ew, that is totally gross.

00:11:04.665 --> 00:11:06.542
Why do you want to go there?

00:11:06.542 --> 00:11:10.504
I know someone who wants mirror
cubes like the one we brought back.

00:11:10.504 --> 00:11:14.466
It's not like we can get any more.
We're lucky we got that one.

00:11:14.466 --> 00:11:16.552
I know how to get them.

00:11:16.552 --> 00:11:17.845
You do?

00:11:17.845 --> 00:11:20.055
We'll hunt those... wiggle-waggles, was it?

00:11:20.055 --> 00:11:21.014
What?

00:11:21.014 --> 00:11:21.974
--You want to hunt those things that
drive people mad just by looking at them?

00:11:21.974 --> 00:11:24.560
--Ding! Ding!
--You want to hunt those things that
drive people mad just by looking at them?

00:11:26.812 --> 00:11:28.105
Yep, them.

00:11:28.105 --> 00:11:29.106
Hunt them?

00:11:29.106 --> 00:11:31.525
We could make some good money, partner.

00:11:31.525 --> 00:11:32.901
Seriously?

00:11:32.901 --> 00:11:33.277
Seriously.

00:11:33.277 --> 00:11:33.944
"Rock Salt (Value Pack)"
Seriously.

00:11:33.944 --> 00:11:35.696
"Rock Salt (Value Pack)"
I bought plenty of ammo.

00:11:35.696 --> 00:11:35.904
I bought plenty of ammo.

00:11:35.904 --> 00:11:39.199
No can do. I nearly died last time.

00:11:39.199 --> 00:11:42.953
True, you looked like a drowned rat.

00:11:42.953 --> 00:11:45.414
What happened to Ophelia?

00:11:45.414 --> 00:11:50.127
Sorry. It's just, I'll probably
end up dead if I go it alone.

00:11:50.127 --> 00:11:53.922
So I want you to come with me.

00:12:00.429 --> 00:12:02.931
I can't think of anything to say.

00:12:02.931 --> 00:12:06.768
Actually, I don't know what I'm doing here.

00:12:06.768 --> 00:12:12.983
I haven't hung out without anyone in ages.
I don't even know what to say.

00:12:33.086 --> 00:12:33.670
--Ow.

00:12:33.670 --> 00:12:35.297
--Sorry.
--Ow.

00:12:35.297 --> 00:12:36.924
This is it.

00:12:51.522 --> 00:12:52.940
Something wrong?

00:12:52.940 --> 00:12:54.399
Come on.

00:12:54.399 --> 00:12:56.902
O-Okay.

00:13:16.463 --> 00:13:21.051
Um... What exactly are you doing?

00:13:21.051 --> 00:13:26.598
Pressing the elevator buttons in a certain
order will take us to the Otherside.

00:13:26.598 --> 00:13:30.644
You, of all people,
must've heard of this before.

00:13:49.329 --> 00:13:51.915
It tried to get in.

00:13:51.915 --> 00:13:55.377
Yeah, it always tries to
get in on the fifth floor.

00:13:55.377 --> 00:13:57.045
Don't ever let it in.

00:13:57.045 --> 00:13:58.922
Y-Yeah.

00:14:11.101 --> 00:14:15.814
Huh? That's strange.
It was never this dark before.

00:14:15.814 --> 00:14:17.649
C-Close it!

00:14:19.318 --> 00:14:21.361
Wh-What was that?

00:14:22.905 --> 00:14:27.117
Sorry. I may have pressed
the buttons in the wrong order.

00:14:54.061 --> 00:14:56.271
Wait. We're climbing down the ladder?

00:14:56.271 --> 00:15:01.109
Yeah, don't worry. I've never fallen.

00:15:12.621 --> 00:15:14.414
This gun is for you.

00:15:14.414 --> 00:15:17.960
I wish it had a holster or something,
but that's how I found it.

00:15:17.960 --> 00:15:20.254
You found it?

00:15:20.254 --> 00:15:24.383
You can sometimes find them
lying around on this side. Umm...

00:15:24.383 --> 00:15:28.470
Shall I show you how to
load it and use the safety?

00:15:28.470 --> 00:15:29.346
Listen...

00:15:29.346 --> 00:15:31.056
Hmm?

00:15:31.056 --> 00:15:35.894
We only just met, so how can you trust me?

00:15:35.894 --> 00:15:41.984
Well, take the gun, for example.
You didn't report me to the police.

00:15:41.984 --> 00:15:44.278
Can you tell me why?

00:15:44.278 --> 00:15:50.742
I'm not sure. Maybe I didn't
want to ask too many questions.

00:15:50.742 --> 00:15:54.621
That's why I trust you.
It's perfect for partners in crime.

00:15:54.621 --> 00:15:57.833
Did you know that in this world

00:15:57.833 --> 00:16:01.795
partners in crime is the most
intimate relationship there is?

00:16:01.795 --> 00:16:04.339
Partners in crime?

00:16:06.717 --> 00:16:09.970
So where does one find a wiggle-waggle monster?

00:16:09.970 --> 00:16:15.225
Where? If I had to guess,
I'd say the countryside.

00:16:15.225 --> 00:16:18.061
People who visit from the city
often report seeing them

00:16:18.061 --> 00:16:20.189
in rice paddies or at the beach.

00:16:20.189 --> 00:16:21.190
Anywhere else?

00:16:21.190 --> 00:16:24.067
It's not like I'm an expert.

00:16:33.327 --> 00:16:36.246
Wh-Who's that?

00:16:41.960 --> 00:16:43.629
A wiggle-waggle.

00:16:43.629 --> 00:16:44.546
Run!

00:16:44.546 --> 00:16:47.299
No, this is why we're here!

00:16:56.725 --> 00:16:57.643
What?

00:16:57.643 --> 00:16:59.645
It didn't work. That's what!

00:16:59.645 --> 00:17:04.274
That's weird. It worked like a charm last time.

00:17:10.906 --> 00:17:13.283
Uh-oh, guns don't work either.

00:17:13.283 --> 00:17:16.286
M-My legs are giving out. How about you?

00:17:16.286 --> 00:17:18.497
Not good.

00:17:18.497 --> 00:17:21.792
T-Toriko, let's assess the situation.

00:17:21.792 --> 00:17:25.504
Well, we can't get up, so we can't get away.

00:17:25.504 --> 00:17:30.175
We're all dizzy, and rock salt and
guns have no effect. What else?

00:17:30.175 --> 00:17:33.303
Well, when I look at it,
I feel like I'm going mad.

00:17:33.303 --> 00:17:36.056
Like you're going mad?
Could you be more specific?

00:17:36.056 --> 00:17:38.433
Like something terrible would happen
if I wrapped my brain around it.

00:17:38.433 --> 00:17:41.103
Wrap your brain around it?
Could you be more specific?

00:17:41.103 --> 00:17:44.606
Enough already! It's just bad news!

00:17:45.732 --> 00:17:49.361
Wait. Last time, I figured it
out in the nick of time.

00:17:49.361 --> 00:17:55.117
Right before it bore down on me,
I didn't avert my eyes.

00:17:55.117 --> 00:17:57.369
If we keep looking at it without
averting our eyes, then maybe...

00:17:57.369 --> 00:17:59.663
What? But I thought
looking at it drives you mad?

00:17:59.663 --> 00:18:02.541
We fought it off before, didn't we?

00:18:02.541 --> 00:18:06.128
That time, the situation had gotten even worse.

00:18:06.128 --> 00:18:07.963
If we just do what we did then, maybe...

00:18:07.963 --> 00:18:09.715
Even if we go mad?

00:18:09.715 --> 00:18:12.176
To hunt creatures on the Otherside,

00:18:12.176 --> 00:18:17.097
we'll have to follow the rules
and logic here. That means...

00:18:17.097 --> 00:18:20.684
We have to stick with it
until the last possible second.

00:18:20.684 --> 00:18:21.894
Count me in!

00:18:21.894 --> 00:18:23.437
No, Toriko, don't look.

00:18:23.437 --> 00:18:24.479
Why not?

00:18:24.479 --> 00:18:29.234
We won't be able to get home if we both go mad.

00:18:29.234 --> 00:18:34.781
So the moment it looks like I can't
handle any more, I'll need your help.

00:18:34.781 --> 00:18:37.701
Okay. I'll figure something out!

00:18:37.701 --> 00:18:39.578
Thanks.

00:18:43.457 --> 00:18:47.503
See? Just a little longer, Sorawo,
and you'll understand.

00:18:47.503 --> 00:18:49.671
Sorawo's so smart, after all.

00:18:49.671 --> 00:18:50.506
Come here.

00:18:50.506 --> 00:18:54.468
I-I heard a story from my kid brother.

00:18:54.468 --> 00:18:56.428
It was around the time when
everything was lush and green.

00:18:56.428 --> 00:19:01.099
What was that person, person,
person dressed in white, white

00:19:01.099 --> 00:19:01.600
--doing in a place like that?

00:19:01.600 --> 00:19:02.768
--See? Try to understand.
Now, try to understand.
--doing in a place like that?

00:19:02.768 --> 00:19:09.274
--See? Try to understand.
Now, try to understand.
--A-A-And that guy bending his joints
in a really weird way is now, now, now...

00:19:09.274 --> 00:19:12.152
On the verge of noon, at that
exact moment, moment, suddenly,

00:19:12.152 --> 00:19:13.487
I'm certain that's when it surged up.

00:19:13.487 --> 00:19:18.325
The incredibly high gray sea that
scraped across the tatami in bare feet...

00:19:27.835 --> 00:19:30.838
I see.

00:19:30.838 --> 00:19:32.923
Toriko threw the rock salt.

00:19:32.923 --> 00:19:35.676
It scored a direct hit.

00:19:35.676 --> 00:19:39.388
The wiggle-waggle was there. Why?

00:19:39.388 --> 00:19:42.182
It was there because I saw it
and recognized it for what it was.

00:19:42.182 --> 00:19:45.435
The rock salt scored a
direct hit because it was there.

00:19:45.435 --> 00:19:49.273
Huh, that's it? It's so obvious.

00:19:49.273 --> 00:19:52.526
There'd be nothing there if I was unaware of it.

00:19:52.526 --> 00:19:55.153
I got it! I got it! I got it!

00:19:55.153 --> 00:19:57.281
Sorawo!

00:19:59.449 --> 00:20:04.204
I don't know what happened,
but whatever you got, it's too much!

00:20:04.204 --> 00:20:08.750
Huh. She's nicer than I thought.

00:20:08.750 --> 00:20:11.378
Snap out of it!

00:20:15.382 --> 00:20:17.009
Toriko, shoot it!

00:20:17.009 --> 00:20:20.512
We can hit it if I look at it and you shoot!

00:20:52.211 --> 00:20:53.795
So there was one.

00:20:53.795 --> 00:20:55.297
Yeah.

00:21:11.605 --> 00:21:15.734
That was so scary! Like, super scary!

00:21:18.070 --> 00:21:21.490
Hey, Sorawo, let's celebrate when we get back!

00:21:21.490 --> 00:21:22.366
Huh?

00:21:22.366 --> 00:21:25.702
We'll have some money to spend, so let's party!

00:21:30.999 --> 00:21:32.876
Oh, why not?

00:21:32.876 --> 00:21:34.711
Yay!

00:21:36.380 --> 00:21:40.926
I wanted to keep the Otherside to myself.

00:21:40.926 --> 00:21:48.058
I still felt that way even after
I discovered how strange and scary it was.

00:21:48.058 --> 00:21:51.687
But now, I'm starting to think

00:21:51.687 --> 00:21:57.359
it might be fun to experience
the place with that weirdo I met.

00:21:58.068 --> 00:22:02.030
"Wiggle-Waggle Hunting"

00:23:32.037 --> 00:23:32.538
"Episode 1 Celebration"

00:23:32.538 --> 00:23:33.747
"Episode 1 Celebration"
Cheers!

00:23:33.747 --> 00:23:34.706
Speaking of which,

00:23:34.706 --> 00:23:35.040
--that value pack of rock salt Toriko
bought without thinking didn't do a thing.

00:23:35.040 --> 00:23:37.709
--This <i>yakitori </i>is so good!
I'm gonna try two skewers at once!
--that value pack of rock salt Toriko
bought without thinking didn't do a thing.

00:23:37.709 --> 00:23:39.044
--This <i>yakitori </i>is so good!
I'm gonna try two skewers at once!
--It was a complete waste.
Grumble, grumble, grumble.

00:23:39.044 --> 00:23:40.504
--Sorawo, careful you don't use any
